🚀 Feature
Add default forward() methods for nn.ModuleList and nn.ModuleDict that returns list/dict of item-wise forward.
Motivation
At several places in my projects, I have code like the following:
class NetworkHeads(nn.ModuleList):
    def forward(self, x):
        return [module(x) for module in self]

or like
class TaskHeads(nn.ModuleDict):
    def forward(self, x):
        return {key: module(x) for key, module in self.items()}

The classes NetworkHeads and TaskHeads are necessary since ModuleList and ModuleDict doesn't come with their own forward methods. Although being only 3 lines long, these classes are slightly annoying.
Proposal
I believe that my use case above might be very common. Could it make sense to define such forward methods by default in these containers?

